     "state"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "The legislature makes laws, the executive carries them out and the judiciary interprets laws and settles disputes. The Supreme Court, High Courts and district courts form the judicial system.\nIndia has three tiers of government: Union, State and local. Decentralisation means sharing power with lower levels so decisions are made close to the people.\nA state is a land with people and a government, but the government can change after elections while the state continues."
    }
